[3] convention (also the brief the builders get, `<scratchpad>/p215/brief.md`):
- notes, logs, verdicts, JSON: token swap by table, nothing else on the line;
- scripts keep their variable names; the repo root is `BMA_REPO` or, absent, the script's own location; the scratch directory is `BMA_SCRATCH` (required, clear error); the tool's config directory is the tool's own `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` or `~/.claude`; the project key is computed from the root the way the tool computes it;
- `BMA_REPO` exists for one reason: a closed round's transcripts hold the path the repo had when it ran, and after the `src/` move (21.7) the script's own location will no longer be that path;
- a regex that *matches* a trace word is rebuilt from those values and reported as a functional line for VERIFY;
- 21.1 only (the live apparatus): the shell entry points source a gitignored `local.env` beside them, so the user's launch command stays one line.
→ next: delegate.

[4] delegation — three builders in parallel, disjoint files, **Sonnet**: the work is a table swap and one repeated edit pattern over 90 files; no finding is judged, no design is chosen (both are fixed in [3]). Split by what can break: (X) scripts of `work/13`–`19`, records, parse-check only; (Y) scripts of `work/20`, same; (Z) `work/21` scripts — the apparatus verified on 2026-11-12, regression by its own `selftest.sh` and `dryrun.sh` (stub only) — plus the 19 non-script files. VERIFY afterwards by an agent that did none of it.
→ next: read the three reports; residue search over the whole tree; then VERIFY.

